  "network": {
    "status": "host-only",
    "note": "rtl8139 on the persistent tap winxprn0, enslaved to the OFFLINE retronet bridge vmbr-rn (streamhost/stations/winxp/rn-tapnet.sh, called `up` from the launcher on every start). Guest on DHCP (reserved 10.99.0.18/24, DNS 10.99.0.2, NO router option -> no default route) behind the fail-closed WINXPRN-IN guard chain - reaches ONLY the gateway CT 10.99.0.2, where IE8 browses the period corpus on :80 seamlessly (wildcard DNS, no proxy configured) and ICQ 2001b signs UIN 51000 in to the OSCAR gateway on :5190; never labhost, the LAN, the gallery or the internet. Windows Firewall stays ON (every profile) with inbound ICMP echo allowed and NO program exception for ICQ - the OSCAR link is outbound-only, so `netstat -n` in the guest shows exactly one connection, 10.99.0.18:* -> 10.99.0.2:5190. Swapped 2026-08-23 from the pre-retronet slirp `-netdev user` (docs/lab/retronet/WEB-STATION-winxp.md, docs/lab/retronet/ICQ-STATION-winxp.md)"
  },
  "retronet": {
    "planes": ["web", "icq"],
    "address": "10.99.0.18",
    "addressing": "dhcp",
    "link": "tap winxprn0 on vmbr-rn",
    "guard": "WINXPRN-IN",
    "joined": "2026-08-23",
    "doc": "docs/lab/retronet/WEB-STATION-winxp.md"
  },
